  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should test the core multimodal hypothesis with a strong, well-balanced configuration to establish a high baseline and reduce uncertainty about whether multimodal fusion (RNA + image) with multiprofile transformer aggregation is the right direction. config_022 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) pairs a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) with a solid, well-established image encoder (resnet50), uses transformer aggregation to handle multiprofile structure, and applies a simple concat fusion. This tests whether the combination of both modalities and multiprofile aggregation yields a strong signal. It is a moderate-cost choice: multimodal + multiprofile + transformer adds overhead, but resnet50 is substantially cheaper than ViT-L, keeping this in the mid-range of expected GPU hours. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can exploit the direction by swapping in ViT-L, weighted fusion, or scgpt; if it underperforms, we learn that the multimodal or aggregation strategy needs rethinking. This is the best use of experiment 1 because it maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design axis (multimodal vs. single-modality) while setting a competitive accuracy bar within the 10-experiment budget."
}

